<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3709" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρωτήριον</span></b> , τό,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>topmost</i> or <i>prominent part</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῦ οὔρεος</span> mountain <i>peak</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.217
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.7
			</span></i>; of a cup, <i>projecting part</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1024a25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>cape, promontory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>end</i> or <i>extremity</i> of anything, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. νεός</span>
			<i>ornament of</i> ship's <i>stern-</i> or <i>stem-post</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.121
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.3.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				5.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				1116
			</span></i> (Delph.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρωτήρια πρύμνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					33.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pl.,
				<i>extremities of body, hands and feet, fingers and toes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Acut.</u>
				59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀ. τῆς Νίκης</span> her
				<i>wings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.121
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.652<i>A</i>23
			</span></i>: sg., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				772b36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in temples,
			etc., statues or ornaments placed on the angles of a pediment, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				116d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				80
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.1484.102
			</span></i> (Epid.); generally, <i>pediment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				63
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
